{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and Lateralus feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want to explore more of Tool's intricate rhythms and immersive sound right now.",
    "City of Evil and Vol. 3 fit because they combine aggressive guitars with melody, connecting with my interest in In Flames and Disturbed."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Make Believe feels off for today's mood: my earlier rock listening does not mean I currently want something lighter than the heavier albums I have been choosing.",
    "Iowa fits my taste for intensity, but intensity alone is not enough today; I would choose something with more melody or the rhythmic complexity that draws me to Tool."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in heavy music seems to have been treated as making thrash, raw aggression, and progressive metal equally appealing right now.",
    "My older alternative rock choices seem to carry more weight than they should when my latest listening makes another Tool album especially appealing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice, 10.000 Days, reflects a current desire to explore Tool more deeply, which makes Aenima and Lateralus stand out above other albums I might enjoy.",
    "I care about how heaviness combines with melody and intricate rhythms; a broadly compatible heavy album can still be a lower priority today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations capture my broad taste for heavy music, but only some reflect my current interest in Tool and in heaviness balanced with melody or rhythmic complexity."
}"}
